Add a third internal fullscreen mode, FSMODE_FULLSCREEN_DECORATOR, that occupies
the whole monitor exactly like FSMODE_FULLSCREEN but keeps window decorations
rendering. Purpose: let a window (opted in per-window) go full-monitor fullscreen
while a decoration-based background effect (hyprglass liquid glass, drawn at
DECORATION_LAYER_BOTTOM) survives. Upstream drops ALL decorations for a true-
fullscreen window (src/render/Renderer.cpp:597, internal != FSMODE_FULLSCREEN),
so such an effect can never survive true fullscreen; maximize keeps decorations
but does not cover the bar/gaps.

Trigger is a plain window tag: a window tagged `decorate_fullscreen` that would
go FSMODE_FULLSCREEN is upgraded to FSMODE_FULLSCREEN_DECORATOR in
setFullscreenMode (post-clamp; tag-only, not raw-dispatcher reachable). The
client mode is left untouched so the app is still told plain fullscreen.

Differences from FSMODE_FULLSCREEN, all deliberate:
  - decorations render      : free, mode 3 != FSMODE_FULLSCREEN at Renderer.cpp:597
  - no border               : mode added to the border/groupbar/border-size gates
  - rounding off            : mode added to Renderer.cpp dontRound
  - stays composited        : direct-scanout (Monitor.cpp) and alphaFullscreen
                              (Window.cpp) LEFT UNCHANGED, so the surface stays
                              translucent and the compositor keeps compositing it,
                              which is what lets the bottom-layer effect show.

fsCovers(mode) (added to the enum header) folds "true fullscreen OR decorator"
into every coverage/layout/scanout/input/protocol site that must treat the new
mode as full-monitor. isFullscreen(window) with a nullopt mode already returns
`internal != FSMODE_NONE` (FullscreenHandler.cpp:54), so hy3 (which only calls
the controller helpers) needs no patch. The built-in scrolling layout is NOT
updated on purpose (this host runs hy3; the scrolling handler never executes).

Same behaviour on hyprland main as of 2026-09-09; line numbers are 0.56.x.

